           receives a BREAK character it advances through the list, which is
           treated as if it were circular.

           Baud rates should be specified in descending order, so that the
           null character (Ctrl-@) can also be used for baud-rate switching.

           This argument is optional and unnecessary for vviirrttuuaall tteerrmmiinnaallss.

           The default for sseerriiaall tteerrmmiinnaallss is keep the current baud rate (see
           ----kkeeeepp--bbaauudd) and if unsuccessful then default to '9600'.

