       This section shows examples for the process field of an entry in the
       _/_e_t_c_/_i_n_i_t_t_a_b file. You’ll have to prepend appropriate values for the
       other fields. See iinniittttaabb(5) for more details.

       For a hardwired line or a console tty:

          //ssbbiinn//aaggeettttyy 99660000 ttttyySS11

       For a directly connected terminal without proper carrier-detect wiring
       (try this if your terminal just sleeps instead of giving you a
       password: prompt):

          //ssbbiinn//aaggeettttyy ----llooccaall--lliinnee 99660000 ttttyySS11 vvtt110000

       For an old-style dial-in line with a 9600/2400/1200 baud modem:

          //ssbbiinn//aaggeettttyy ----eexxttrraacctt--bbaauudd ----ttiimmeeoouutt 6600 ttttyySS11 99660000,,22440000,,11220000

       For a Hayes modem with a fixed 115200 bps interface to the machine (the
