BBUUGGSS
       The baud-rate detection feature (the ----eexxttrraacctt--bbaauudd option) requires
       that aaggeettttyy be scheduled soon enough after completion of a dial-in call
       (within 30 ms with modems that talk at 2400 baud). For robustness,
       always use the ----eexxttrraacctt--bbaauudd option in combination with a multiple
       baud rate command-line argument, so that BREAK processing is enabled.

       The text in the _/_e_t_c_/_i_s_s_u_e file (or other) and the login prompt are
       always output with 7-bit characters and space parity.

       The baud-rate detection feature (the ----eexxttrraacctt--bbaauudd option) requires
       that the modem emits its status message _a_f_t_e_r raising the DCD line.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
       Depending on how the program was configured, all diagnostics are
       written to the console device or reported via the ssyysslloogg(3) facility.
       Error messages are produced if the _p_o_r_t argument does not specify a
       terminal device; if there is no utmp entry for the current process
       (System V only); and so on.

